{% comment %}
  Contrarian Product Rules — notice placement anchor.

  This block previously shipped debug scaffolding to the storefront: a literal
  "THIS IS THE NEW CPR BLOCK" heading and a <pre> dump of the raw rules
  metafield, both visible to customers on every product page.

  The customer-facing notices are rendered by product-rules.js, which is loaded
  by the app embed block (product-rules-embed.liquid) and injects the
  .cpr-preorder and [data-cpr-pickup-notice] elements itself. Rendering the same
  copy here would show every notice twice, so this block deliberately emits no
  visible content — it only marks the position in the product section where a
  merchant wants the notice to appear.

  The block is kept rather than deleted so that themes which already have it
  placed do not break on update.
{% endcomment %}

<div
  class="cpr-notice-anchor"
  data-cpr-notice-anchor
  data-cpr-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  hidden
></div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product rule notice",
  "target": "section",
  "templates": ["product"],
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
